# Delvers S3E10 — Sad in a boney kind of way: P/Q ASR comparison (2026-10-26)

**Source-identity follow-up, 2026-10-27:** [Recorded-blob verification](DELVERS_S3E10_SOURCE_IDENTITY_2026-10-27.md) establishes exact equality after CRLF-to-LF conversion only and matching source paths in the recorded initial local commit. Raw local byte identity is false because of line endings. The earlier claim that commit correspondence was unestablished remains dated history; it is now resolved for those two source paths, without identifying the precise historical/default remote branch tip. The 1,529/19,536 text-disagreement result is not recomputed or upgraded to accuracy, additional interpretation or listening verification.

[Played source-first dossier](../delvers/episodes/S3E10.md). **19,536 vs 19,626 words; 1,529 ordered word edits = 7.83% inter-ASR TEXT difference**, NOT WER, audio truth, confirmed omissions/hallucinations, or relative accuracy. **Remote P blob `0a42f9d16de8e3b1a2f8f0cfb5d79b05e7351eee`**, **2,146 cues**, ending **02:34:03.200**; **remote Q blob `40be0079e42b01b147c975b40c5edafd7d99d281`**, **3,480 cues**, ending **02:34:02.860**; **Q has 90 more normalized tokens and ends 0.340sec earlier**, its opening begins 7.28sec earlier than P. Source files: [P](../sources/Delvers%20S3E10.%20Sad%20in%20a%20boney%20kind%20of%20way.parakeet.processed.srt) · [Q](../sources/Delvers%20S3E10.%20Sad%20in%20a%20boney%20kind%20of%20way.qwen-q8.canary-ctc.nemotron.srt).

**Reproducible metric method:** Parse full chronological SRT cue blocks and concatenate spoken cue text; exclude cue IDs, timestamp lines and literal `(speaker N)` labels; lowercase, delete straight/curly apostrophes so contractions join, replace non-Unicode-letter/digit characters with whitespace, split words. Two-row dynamic programming Levenshtein with unit insertion/deletion/substitution costs and ±4,700-word-index band gives **1,529**. As optimum below 4,700, it cannot have an out-of-band cheaper path; hence exactly global unrestricted score. This is **not audio time-alignment** and doesn't identify actual false words.

**Provenance:** Initial connected local repository `main` at **`0df6f7ca95fc76d3ba976d28c9ef727450b2f701`**, ONE unrelated modified Stanley illustration report, **no SRT changes**. Both HEAD-pinned GitHub fetches **404**, so full P/Q exports fetched from **GitHub DEFAULT branch** and recorded by remote blob IDs. First TEN local SRT lines of each independently checked against corresponding remote beginnings; **whole-file local-remote byte equivalence NOT established**, cannot claim these remote blobs belong to local HEAD. P text read chronologically in 5-minute recording clock ranges **0–40, 40–80, 80–125, 125–155** incl credits; full Q parsed computationally and selected independent Q excerpts **0–10, 37–42, 49–59, 63–73, 77–84, 88–105, 108–117, 133–145, 144–154**, some large excerpts output-truncated; NOT an independently exhaustive Q story reading. **NO original MP3/audio listened to; no Discord maps/character sheets/official documentation checked.** Model names are filename-derived only.

